The invoices related to the Services as per the agreement must comply with the GST law and include the following details: 

(a) A reference to the agreement;
(b) The relevant purchase order number;
(c) The Contractor’s Australian Business Number (if applicable);
(d) The Contract Price due to the Contractor and the basis for its calculation;
(e) The amount of any GST paid or payable by ASC Shipbuilding with respect to the Contract Price;
(f) The date(s) of delivery of the Services;
(g) A description of the Services delivered; and
(h) The Contractor’s details for payment.

Invoices should be submitted to the Accounts Payable Department by email to ap.helpdesk@baesystems.com, with a copy to the ASC Shipbuilding Representative as specified in the Schedule. Payment for correctly invoiced amounts will be made by the end of the month following the month in which the invoice is received, provided that the invoice is certified by the ASC Shipbuilding Representative as correctly calculated with respect to Services satisfactorily completed.

The Contractor must comply with the following Commonwealth policies relevant to this Agreement: 

1. Conflicts of interest; 
2. Gifts, hospitality and sponsorship; 
3. Notification of post separation employment; 
4. Management and reporting of unacceptable behaviour; 
5. Incident reporting and management policies as detailed in the DPPM, DI(G) PERS 25-6, DI(G) PERS 25-7,DI(G) PERS 25-4, DI(G) PERS 35-3 and Interim Defence Instruction ADMIN 45-2;
6. Australian Defence Force alcohol policy as detailed in DI(G) PERS 15-1; 
7. Public Interest Disclosure policy as detailed at: http://www.ombudsman.gov.au/Our-responsibilities/making-a-disclosure.
